# Boot configuration for the gateway container. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# This is the SERVER's config: the provider keys it spends against, and the
# admin password for the proxy. It is NOT how you authenticate as a caller —
# that is a virtual key, and it lives in `.vkey`. Keeping the two apart is the
# point of the whole exercise: the real provider key never leaves this host,
# and a developer only ever holds a virtual key.
#
# `.env` and `.vkey` are both gitignored. Never commit either.
#
# docker-compose.yml reads every variable below and documents each one next to
# the code that uses it. It is the authoritative list.

# --- Required — the stack refuses to start without these two ---------------

# Real Anthropic key from https://platform.claude.com, with credit on it.
# This is a developer-platform account: NOT a claude.ai subscription, and
# upgrading claude.ai to Pro does not produce one.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Admin password for the proxy and its UI at http://localhost:4000/ui.
# Not issued by anyone — choose a strong string. You need it to mint virtual
# keys. Rotating it invalidates every existing virtual key.
LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=

# --- Optional — non-Anthropic providers ------------------------------------
#
# All four are optional. An Anthropic-only setup boots fine with every one of
# them blank; the routes that need them simply return an upstream error when
# called. Add a key only for the routes you actually want.
# See ../docs/NON-ANTHROPIC-MODELS.md.

# Free-tier aggregator routes (nemotron, minimax, gemma, ...).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Groq — the gpt-oss routes. These are OpenAI's OPEN-WEIGHT models served by
# Groq, which is not the same thing as the first-party OpenAI route below.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# OpenAI — first party. Account is on limited credit; see config.yaml.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# z.ai — first party. The Flash models are free on z.ai's own price list (not
# expiring trial credit), so this needs an account but no card.
ZAI_API_KEY=

# --- Not set here on purpose -----------------------------------------------
#
# OLLAMA_API_BASE and the GATEWAY_* behaviour knobs all have working defaults
# in docker-compose.yml, so they are omitted rather than blanked — an empty
# value here would override a good default with nothing. To change one, add it
# explicitly and see ../docs/GATEWAY-MODIFY.md for what it does.
#
# NOTE: `docker compose restart` reuses the container's baked-in environment.
# After editing .env you need `up -d` — which is what ./gateway-up.sh runs.
